  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Priory Register",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Priory Register\"**\n\nThe site is a quiet institutional register set inside a mandatory frame. The frame (red top bar, the official flag banner photograph with the full Czech name in white capitals, the graphite menu bar, and the grey / white / red footer) is the Grand Magistry \"Entities Theme\": it is brand, not a design choice, and it is reproduced, never reinterpreted. Inside the frame the Grand Priory speaks plainly: white and pale-grey bands, hairline-ruled definition lists, EB Garamond headings and Asap text, real photographs at the Order's 800×470 basic image ratio.\n\nInformation is set as records rather than cards: facts, service times, works, news and downloads are all rows between 1px hairlines, with a label column and a value column. Density is moderate and generous to older readers (17px body, 1.65 leading, 44px targets). Red is the Order's colour and is kept scarce inside the frame: links, the single filled button, the active-state underline and focus rings.\n\nThe system rejects the charity-landing vocabulary (hero slogan, donate button, card grid) and any ornament standing in for the Order's identity. Dignity comes from structure, type and authentic photography.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Mandatory Grand Magistry frame, reproduced exactly on every page.",
      "White / #f3f3f3 alternating bands, flat, separated only by tone and hairlines.",
      "Rows, not cards: two-column definition lists between hairline rules.",
      "EB Garamond for headings and row titles; Asap for everything functional.",
      "Red reserved for frame, links, the one filled button, active state and focus.",
      "Motion is short, settling and fully suppressed under reduced motion."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Red Is Signal Rule",
        "body": "Inside the frame, red appears only as link text, the single filled button per page, an active-state underline or rule, and focus. Never as a band, a card fill or a heading colour.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Grey Ground Rule",
        "body": "On a #f3f3f3 band, every red text link switches to Text Red. Magistry Red text on grey fails AA.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Voices Rule",
        "body": "Garamond speaks for the Priory (headings, row titles, the calendar years, pull quotes in italic). Asap carries everything a visitor operates or scans: menus, dates, times, labels, buttons, tables. Never set Garamond in uppercase or in UI chrome.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Times Rule",
        "body": "Service times, dates and table numbers use tabular figures.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Hairline, Not Shadow Rule",
        "body": "Separate content with 1px #c7c7c7 rules and band tone. Cards, raised panels and hover lifts are not part of this system.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** reproduce the Grand Magistry frame (top bar, official banner photograph with full Czech name, graphite menu, grey / white / red footer) unchanged on every page.",
      "**Do** set lists of facts, times, works and news as hairline-ruled rows with a muted label column.",
